    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"id\": \"5609690caaf546c0\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"### Minimum radius for 2 neighbours, by station\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"For each station, the smallest radius R such that at least 2 other\\n\",\n",
    "    \"stations fall within it -- equivalently, the distance to its\\n\",\n",
    "    \"**second**-nearest neighbour (the first-nearest alone isn't enough to\\n\",\n",
    "    \"satisfy the ≥2-neighbours criterion used in the plot below).\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"id\": \"25c2039f326147d4\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {\n",
    "    \"ExecuteTime\": {\n",
    "     \"end_time\": \"2026-09-02T10:37:09.141792Z\",\n",
    "     \"start_time\": \"2026-09-02T10:37:09.130239Z\"\n",
    "    }\n",
    "   },\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"# ── Minimum radius for 2 neighbours, by station ─────────────────────────────\\n\",\n",
    "    \"DIST_SORTED = np.sort(DIST, axis=1)          # (N, N), ascending, self excluded (inf)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"min_r_2nn = DIST_SORTED[:, 1]                # distance to 2nd-nearest neighbour\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"df_min_r = pd.DataFrame({\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    \\\"station\\\": stn.abbr.values,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    \\\"min_radius_2nn_km\\\": min_r_2nn,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"}).sort_values(\\\"min_radius_2nn_km\\\", ascending=False).reset_index(drop=True)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(f\\\"Minimum radius for \\\\u22652 neighbours, by station \\\"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"      f\\\"(median={np.median(min_r_2nn):.1f} km, \\\"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"      f\\\"max={min_r_2nn.max():.1f} km):\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"#display(df_min_r.style.format({\\\"min_radius_2nn_km\\\": \\\"{:.1f}\\\"}))\\n\"\n",
    "   ],\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"id\": \"9d26736d8ef94934\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"## MAE at +3h lead vs distance to k-th nearest neighbour — Dense vs Spatially Blind, by terrain class\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Simplified to the two extremes of neighbour distance (1st and 5th\\n\",\n",
    "    \"nearest) and the two MR=0.0 architecture endpoints: Dense (v31, full\\n\",\n",
    "    \"spatial attention) vs Spatially Blind (v32-blind, no spatial\\n\",\n",
    "    \"attention). Marker shape distinguishes the model, colour distinguishes\\n\",\n",
    "    \"terrain class, and a Pearson-r regression line is fit per model. If\\n\",\n",
    "    \"spatial attention is what drives the isolation effect, Dense should\\n\",\n",
    "    \"show a real trend while Spatially Blind should not.\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"id\": \"suppl_bins\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {\n",
    "    \"ExecuteTime\": {\n",
    "     \"end_time\": \"2026-09-02T10:37:10.247583Z\",\n",
    "     \"start_time\": \"2026-09-02T10:37:09.143309Z\"\n",
    "    }\n",
    "   },\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"# ── MAE at +3h lead vs distance to k-th nearest neighbour — Dense vs Spatially Blind, by terrain class ──\\n\",\n",
    "    \"_, COL_DENSE, _ = C.MODELS[\\\"v31\\\"]\\n\",\n",
    "    \"_, COL_BLIND, _ = C.MODELS[\\\"v32-blind\\\"]\\n\",\n",
    "    \"MRK_DENSE, MRK_BLIND = \\\"o\\\", \\\"^\\\"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"a_dense = AGG[\\\"v31\\\"]\\n\",\n",
    "    \"cnt_d = a_dense[\\\"mod_all_cnt\\\"][REF_KI, :, :]\\n\",\n",
    "    \"sum_d = a_dense[\\\"mod_all_sum_phys\\\"][REF_KI, :, :]\\n\",\n",
    "    \"mae_dense = np.where(cnt_d > 0, sum_d / np.maximum(cnt_d, 1), np.nan)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"a_blind = AGG[\\\"v32-blind\\\"]\\n\",\n",
    "    \"cnt_b = a_blind[\\\"mod_all_cnt\\\"][REF_KI, :, :]\\n\",\n",
    "    \"sum_b = a_blind[\\\"mod_all_sum_phys\\\"][REF_KI, :, :]\\n\",\n",
    "    \"mae_blind = np.where(cnt_b > 0, sum_b / np.maximum(cnt_b, 1), np.nan)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"K_NEIGHBOURS = [1, 5]\\n\",\n",
    "    \"K_ORDINAL = {1: \\\"1st\\\", 5: \\\"5th\\\"}\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"tc_of_station = np.full(N, \\\"\\\", dtype=object)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"for tc in C.TCLASSES:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    tc_of_station[TC_IDX[tc]] = tc\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"def _fit_line(ax, x, y, color):\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    \\\"\\\"\\\"Pearson-r linear fit, drawn + returned in the given colour.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    valid = np.isfinite(x) & np.isfinite(y)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    if valid.sum() < 5 or x[valid].std() == 0:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        return None\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    slope, intercept, r, p, _ = linregress(x[valid], y[valid])\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    xfit = np.linspace(x[valid].min(), x[valid].max(), 50)\\n\",\n",
