    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"id\": \"9742d4896e05425b\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"### Neighbour loss for visible stations (R=25 / 50 / 100 km)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Even though a visible station's own observations are available, its\\n\",\n",
    "    \"*neighbours* may still be masked under MR=0.5. This counts, for each\\n\",\n",
    "    \"visible station, how many of its R-km neighbours were masked by the\\n\",\n",
    "    \"same fixed evaluation mask — the indirect information loss that could\\n\",\n",
    "    \"explain part of the MR=0.0 vs MR=0.5 gap above via reduced cross-station\\n\",\n",
    "    \"attention context, independent of the target station's own masking\\n\",\n",
    "    \"status.\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"id\": \"04c52b4b00674cf6\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {\n",
    "    \"ExecuteTime\": {\n",
    "     \"end_time\": \"2026-09-02T10:37:14.890928Z\",\n",
    "     \"start_time\": \"2026-09-02T10:37:14.754526Z\"\n",
    "    }\n",
    "   },\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"# ── Neighbour loss for visible stations due to masking (R=25/50/100 km) ──────\\n\",\n",
    "    \"NEIGHBOUR_RADII = [25, 50, 100]\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"means, stds, fracs = [], [], []\\n\",\n",
    "    \"for R in NEIGHBOUR_RADII:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    lmc = local_masked_count[R][visible_bool]                       # (n_obs,)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    n_loc = np.broadcast_to(N_LOCAL[R][None, :], visible_bool.shape)[visible_bool]\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    frac = lmc / np.maximum(n_loc, 1)\\n\",\n",
